# The X search engine's session - app/search/engines/xsearch.py.
# Loaded by api/app/config.py. A real environment variable always wins over this file, and
# this file is read once at startup, so a rotated cookie takes a restart.
#
# Both values are the cookies of an already logged-in https://x.com session. The account is
# the identity every search is made as, so it should be a throwaway one: search is a read
# that a rate limiter counts, and a 429 costs a token its leads.
#   CH_X_AUTH_TOKEN  the session cookie
#   CH_X_CT0         the CSRF token, sent as X-Csrf-Token beside the bearer
#   CH_X_CLI         the search client that carries the session; defaults to `twitter`
#                    (a subprocess on PATH, no model call, no tokens)

# Copy this file to search.env and fill both in from the cookies of a logged-in x.com
# session (DevTools -> Application -> Cookies -> https://x.com). Use a throwaway account.
CH_X_AUTH_TOKEN=
CH_X_CT0=
CH_X_CLI=twitter
